      "worked": "The complete diagonal gives the common sum: $19+15+11=45$.\n\nBottom middle: $45-22-11=12$.\n\nMiddle left: $45-19-22=4$.\n\nTop right: $45-15-22=8$.\n\nTop middle: $45-19-8=18$.\n\nMiddle right: $45-4-15=26$.\n\nCheck: the rows give $19+18+8=45$, $4+15+26=45$ and $22+12+11=45$; the columns give $19+4+22=45$, $18+15+12=45$ and $8+26+11=45$; both diagonals give $45$.",
